WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.829
ALEX: So for anyone building or buying
enterprise AI right now — what

00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:05.657
ALEX: do you do with this?

00:00:05.742 --> 00:00:09.445
RUFUS: You use it as a benchmark.
Whatever agent security tooling you're
currently

00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:13.148
RUFUS: running — software guardrails,
observability platforms — you now have a
hardware-enforced

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:16.851
RUFUS: option to measure against.

00:00:16.961 --> 00:00:20.885
JAMIE: And if you're in a regulated
industry — finance, healthcare, defense
—

00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:24.810
JAMIE: the millisecond quarantine claim
is worth testing seriously, because an
agent acting

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.734
JAMIE: outside its bounds in those
environments is not a theoretical cost.

00:00:28.914 --> 00:00:31.572
ALEX: NVIDIA says the capacity gain is
"up to" 20%, which is a

00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:34.231
ALEX: ceiling, not a floor.
